### L21.S3 · [D] · Rose, Henry
*Purpose: the week's counsel — Monday noon; the steady, the offer's reading; the counsel. (Turns: 8)*
> *(The war room, Monday noon. Henry brings the week's counsel — the steady voice, the plain reading — and the offer looks different through his eyes.)*
> "Fourteen thousand." Henry sets his coffee down. "For twenty-one thousand face. The discount's steep, Rose — steep enough to be a second price wearing a first price's coat."
> (T1 · look closer) *The coffee steams between them — and the steady man's arithmetic is the week's ballast, as always.*
> "The second price is the acknowledgment." Rose sits opposite. "Written in the buyback book — where the market hears. The estate's price: his Dealing recorded straight."
> (T2 · tone) *Level, candid, and grateful — the steady man gets it all, unadorned.*
> "Recorded straight." He drinks. "Rackham — the duelist, the gambler, the man who tried to take your house. And you mean to write him clean in the book, Rose?"
> (T3 · dialogue) *"The book records."; "The man, remembered."; "The price, weighed."*
> "I mean to write what he did." Her voice doesn't lift. "The Dealing — fifteen thousand — sold at honest prices. Six thousand retained and never pressed. If it's true, Henry, the book can carry it."
> (T4 · stance) *Chin up, shoulders back — the heiress holding the line between the debt and the man.*
> Henry nods slowly. "If it's true." He sets the cup down. "That's it, Rose — the *if*. The house doesn't write fiction in its ledgers."
> (T5 · look closer) *The nod is slow, but it's a nod — and the steady man doesn't nod at things he hasn't weighed.*
> "Then we weigh it." Rose stands. "The broker names himself today. Drayton — that's the whisper. We hear him, we weigh him, and then we decide."
> (T6 · dialogue) *"The named, today."; "The weighed, tomorrow."; "The decided, Tuesday."*
> He stands too. "Tuesday." A pause. "The fourteen thousand's the venture's, Rose — twenty-two seven thirty-six becomes eight seven thirty-six. Say it plain before you spend it."
> (T7 · choice) *Say it plain. The spending's honest when the number's spoken first.*
> "Eight thousand, seven hundred and thirty-six." She meets his eyes. "Said plain, Henry. And worth it — if the paper's true."
> (T8 · remembered micro-decision) *The counsel banked, the number spoken — the steady man's arithmetic filed, the week's spending faced.*
> *The noon light on the war room's table — fourteen thousand weighed, the steady man's counsel keeping its level.*
