### L21.S4 · [D] · Rose, Augusta
*Purpose: the dowager on the offer — Monday afternoon; the price unpriced; the formidable. (Turns: 8)*
> *(The dowager's drawing room, Monday afternoon. Augusta receives the week's news — the offer, the acknowledgment, the named — and the formidable listens the way granite listens.)*
> "Drayton." Augusta doesn't waste breath on greetings. "Rackham's broker, named at last. And the price — fourteen thousand pounds, and a paragraph in a book. You call this sound, Rose?"
> (T1 · look closer) *The drawing room is all stillness and silver — and the question lands in it like a dropped coin, ringing.*
> "I call it Rackham's." Rose takes the offered chair. "The paper's his Dealing, Grandmama — fifteen thousand — and six thousand he kept back and traded. The price is the acknowledgment. Written, witnessed, where the market hears."
> (T2 · tone) *Respectful, unflinching, and heiress-clear — the dowager deserves the truth, and the truth deserves its spine.*
> "Written." The formidable leans forward. "You mean to set down, in the house's own book, that Rackham —" she pauses "— dealt straight. The man who broke your father's peace. In ink."
> (T3 · dialogue) *"The book, the ink."; "The man, the dealing."; "The house decides."*
> "If he dealt straight." Rose meets her eyes. "The book records what was done, Grandmama — not what the City gossiped. If the Dealing was honest, the ink can say so."
> (T4 · stance) *Forward in the chair, hands clasped — the granddaughter making her case the way the house taught her: plainly.*
> Augusta studies her for a long moment. "The dead," she says at last, "are convenient, Rose. They can't contradict the paragraph. Remember that when you write it."
> (T5 · look closer) *The warning is the dowager's finest kind: given once, and left to do its work.*
> "Duly remembered." Rose stands. "And Grandmama — the broker names himself today. Drayton. Precise, the whisper says. Unhurried."
> (T6 · dialogue) *"The named, today."; "The precise, the unhurried."; "The house hears."*
> "Unhurried." Augusta rises — a dismissal and a benediction in one movement. "The unhurried are always in a hurry about something, Rose. Find out what."
> (T7 · choice) *Find out what. The dowager's counsel is the week's sharpest instrument — use it.*
> The drawing room door closes behind her — soft, final, the week's first audience done.
> (T8 · remembered micro-decision) *The warning filed, the counsel taken — the formidable's word kept, the broker's hurry sought.*
