> (T6 · dialogue) *"Tomorrow, the answer."; "The estate hears."; "The terms, whole."*
> "It will." Drayton bows — the week's business, paused at its hinge. "Miss Hartwell —" at the door "— the unhurried, your grandmother calls us. She is right. We have waited eleven years. One more night is nothing."
